{
  "zone_maps": {
    "doc": "M2-UI-16/18: the zones the objective system and the field menu's map know. Each zone: its scene (the field's current scene is matched against it), its name_key, its route_index on the pilgrimage strip (Haluna -> the Saltgrass Causeway -> the Shell Shrine), the world rectangle the map shows ([x, z, width, depth] in metres), its shape source (Haluna: its layout JSON; the Shell Shrine: its trial JSON), and its points of interest. A POI is {id, name_key, kind, at: [x, z], source}: `at` is a world position (x east, z south), `source` names where it comes from ('node:<path in the zone scene>' or 'layout:<key in the shape source>'), and tools/tests/test_zone_map_pois.py checks the two agree. Kinds draw as glyphs: shrine, shop, inn, talk, path, door, pool, dock, home. route lists the pilgrimage strip in order; a route stop with no zone is a place the party passes through without a map of its own yet. M3-UI-04: the Act I greybox zones (Ch1, Ch4, Ch5, Ch7, Ch9) are shape_kind greybox_layout: their shapes are the layout's blocks (ZoneMapShapes.greybox_layer), with shape_hints naming blocks by layer where height alone reads them wrong (sea: open water under everything; water, floors, pads, buildings, structures, skip). A greybox zone's scene is only its root, so its POI sources name layout points instead of nodes: 'spawn:<id>', 'trigger:<id>' (the trigger's at), 'actor:<id>' (the actor's at) and 'mark:<id>'. The route runs the whole of Act I; the strip shows only the stops near the current one (zone_map_menu.json route before/after).",
